{"title":"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Alternative_Solution_for_part(a)_with_Inversion\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternative Solution for part(a) with Inversion</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be a point inside acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/e/19e890d3c46af8ae9f9bb0865b5641c6941bbb5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADB = \\angle ACB+\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"172\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/d/96dad4ee92208ad7b907068e9bea17203738ef7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC\\cdot BD=AD\\cdot BC$\" width=\"166\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>(a) Calculate the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cc113fa2d8545ffe906fc0b768f957f1cc37091.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB\\cdot CD}{AC\\cdot BD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>(b) Prove that the tangents at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the circumcircles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311dde11ff2e6480999d8c23b94bb4d7550dde68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/b/15bda2f23a7e2a0c5be295240e1c6dbf6553458e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> are perpendicular.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:IMO_1993_A2.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/51/IMO_1993_A2.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"239\" height=\"303\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\nLet us construct a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c71f19552a05ee5e2b31e94aff3fb986884bf31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> satisfying the following conditions: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/d/68d6caf88be61a3a409de0b6576b27ebe143aac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;, B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"19\" /> are on the same side of AC, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/a/9ba949addc9f396eff050f4e67ac41c893b7c60b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = B&#39;C$\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46a0d8b5f20a86018928a9800a770cf98842e093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCB&#39; = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/51889a83b0163ee1e28588fb83976b139faf8637.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADB \\sim \\triangle ACB&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2fca494c99bd24072df862d53e90af59a0a225b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\frac{AB}{BD} = \\frac{AB&#39;}{B&#39;C}\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Also considering directed angles mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/d/b2d239554d5a7feaf86d5279d6499ea3b97855a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\measuredangle CAB&#39; = \\measuredangle DAB \\implies \\measuredangle CAD = \\measuredangle BAB&#39;\\]\" width=\"330\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/3712e4ecc7a7103b4b3302b4386c68fefb679575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB&#39;}{AB} = \\frac{B&#39;C}{BD} = \\frac{BC}{BD} = \\frac{AC}{AD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"217\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fbd897f47b91300ee59e70ba318d0a37d82fcf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\triangle ABB&#39; \\sim \\triangle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/87940e8971d0bf490da181090b0995ec6c02c7df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CD}{AC} = \\frac{BB&#39;}{AB&#39;}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Finally, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f9050f6cef15bae4d3923f68ffd4a5af55619d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB \\cdot CD}{AC \\cdot BD} = \\frac{BB&#39;}{CB&#39;} = \\boxed{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"199\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>For the second part, let the tangent to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/6703cc61665bb89f2790f6d60122f0c25331adde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ADC)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/72451f73f38f596f3450e2699e9143eaf0391930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DX$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> and the tangent to the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/2/4f2906ff28ace730388f291f238447ddd5a2cfe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ADB)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/521eb037ef25ecef93c9644d789eed0163a05c52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DY$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a53d713efb3d0d0acc6a172692ea47d40c712911.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle ADX = \\measuredangle ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"141\" height=\"14\" /> due to the tangent-chord theorem.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7913f7d10d3f4ee83e688986c2a92577b0755a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle YDB = \\measuredangle DCB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"141\" height=\"14\" /> for the same reason.\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/5318bc1b0d6f9b4f0be43a1f3581f9e979b4cb30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\measuredangle ADX + \\measuredangle YDB = \\measuredangle ACB\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76bb04551e8781ec68ff3033ee91e78142d7000d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\measuredangle ADB = \\measuredangle ACB + 90^{\\circ}\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/855e7a48a01ed1e35c7d2d840e785a6b2ea77bea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\measuredangle ADX + \\measuredangle XDY + \\measuredangle YDB = \\measuredangle ACB + \\measuredangle XDY = \\measuredangle ACB + 90^{\\circ}\\]\" width=\"507\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76a688a200de6c824c5dddf66fa2969cf8eff72b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\measuredangle XDY = 90^{\\circ}\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"13\" /> which means circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/6703cc61665bb89f2790f6d60122f0c25331adde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ADC)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/2/4f2906ff28ace730388f291f238447ddd5a2cfe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ADB)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> are orthogonal.                <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n~reyaansh_agrawal\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Alternative_Solution_for_part.28a.29_with_Inversion\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternative_Solution_for_part(a)_with_Inversion\">Alternative Solution for part(a) with Inversion</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Alternative Solution for part(a) with Inversion\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Invert around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e1630c915bd1b27bfa1f505bf1ac0bb9f5d61f32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545551b3d62c4e23d5df7352a55602d0aa9adcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> denote the image of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> after inversion for all points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3ce33ec2a34dc4fddaec3224043f4a72bbe6d0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> Then, by the properties of inversion, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e9a6a4b24edfb0a0544cf311fe56f79ec5310d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle{ADB}=\\measuredangle{D&#39;B&#39;A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/0/6f02a7afab99b28f34d1aab3a770dc94d0e90478.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle{ACB}=\\measuredangle{C&#39;B&#39;A},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"19\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/f/e5f3c9598810cff127e1a59dbf59f8e4ba40f371.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\measuredangle{ADB}+\\measuredangle{BCA}=\\measuredangle{D&#39;B&#39;A}+\\measuredangle{AB&#39;C&#39;}=\\measuredangle{C&#39;B&#39;D&#39;}=90^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"460\" height=\"15\" />\nAlso, by the Inversion Distance Formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5e3036205882bb843554268c16fe07d00c1986.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AC=\\frac{r^2}{AC&#39;},\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a76edcd3fddb537ef6c47e682433abe0fb713e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BD=\\frac{r^2}{AD&#39;\\cdot AB&#39;}\\cdot B&#39;D&#39;,\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/5/eb5b469808e3323869b2272d1ef817fca707a3bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AD=\\frac{r^2}{AD&#39;},\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da5dc6e25c5aabf32b0de2900220549199f5e24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BC=\\frac{r^2}{AB&#39;\\cdot AC&#39;}\\cdot B&#39;C&#39;.\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"39\" /> Thus, we obtain \n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\nAC\\cdot BD&amp;=AD\\cdot BC\\\\\n\\frac{r^2}{AC'}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{r^2}{AD'\\cdot AB'}\\cdot B'D'\\right)&amp;=\\frac{r^2}{AD'}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{r^2}{AB'\\cdot AC'}\\cdot B'C'\\right)\\\\\nB'D'&amp;=B'C'.\\\\\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Hence, combining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de51c3207996dc57b8109b2fc652d28765e6a94a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;D&#39;=B&#39;C&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2f4a7407d71ebeaac0bec84c0b973905d23dabf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle{C&#39;B&#39;D&#39;}=90^\\circ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"19\" /> we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/b/6ab84680784978897a437b6af27441c921eae911.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{C&#39;D&#39;}{B&#39;D&#39;}=\\sqrt{2}.\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" /> But \n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{C'D'}{B'D'}&amp;=\\frac{\\frac{r^2}{AB'}\\cdot\\frac{r^2}{AC'\\cdot AD'}\\cdot C'D'}{\\frac{r^2}{AC'}\\cdot\\frac{r^2}{AB'\\cdot AD'}\\cdot B'D'}\\\\\n&amp;=\\frac{AB\\cdot CD}{AC\\cdot BD}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>by the Inversion distance formula. Thus, the desired ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b59c23e0e476e060eda5724e6cef03f44e8b7e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\sqrt{2}.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"42\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~ReticulatedPython\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/e/a9e81861124480a61a978b3a2bf96d246544ca49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); defaultpen(fontsize(11pt));  // Angle definitions in radians real deg2rad = pi / 180; real angC = 65 * deg2rad; real angA = 49 * deg2rad; real angB = 66 * deg2rad; // 180 - 65 - 49  // Triangle coordinates (C is at origin, A is on positive x-axis) real scale = 5; pair C = (0,0); pair A = (scale * sin(angB), 0); pair B = (scale * sin(angA) * cos(angC), scale * sin(angA) * sin(angC));  // 1. Apollonius Circle Locus real k = length(B-C) / length(A-C); pair X1 = (B + k*A) / (1 + k); pair X2 = (B - k*A) / (1 - k); pair O1 = (X1 + X2) / 2; real R1 = length(X1 - X2) / 2; path circ1 = circle(O1, R1);  // 2. Subtended Angle Circle Locus real c_len = length(A-B); real R2 = c_len / (2 * cos(angC)); // Using the 90+C property for the radius real d = c_len/2 * tan(angC); pair M = (A+B)/2; pair dir = unit( (-(B.y-A.y), B.x-A.x) ); // Perpendicular direction to AB  pair O2a = M + d * dir; pair O2b = M - d * dir; path circ2a = circle(O2a, R2); path circ2b = circle(O2b, R2);  // Check if a point is strictly inside triangle ABC using cross products bool inTriangle(pair P, pair A, pair B, pair C) {     real cross1 = (P.x - B.x)*(A.y - B.y) - (P.y - B.y)*(A.x - B.x);     real cross2 = (P.x - C.x)*(B.y - C.y) - (P.y - C.y)*(B.x - C.x);     real cross3 = (P.x - A.x)*(C.y - A.y) - (P.y - A.y)*(C.x - A.x);     bool has_neg = (cross1 &lt; -1e-4) || (cross2 &lt; -1e-4) || (cross3 &lt; -1e-4);     bool has_pos = (cross1 &gt; 1e-4)  || (cross2 &gt; 1e-4)  || (cross3 &gt; 1e-4);     return !(has_neg &amp;&amp; has_pos); }  // Find intersections between the Apollonius circle and the two Angle circles pair[] pts1 = intersectionpoints(circ1, circ2a); pair[] pts2 = intersectionpoints(circ1, circ2b); pair[] pts; for (int i = 0; i &lt; pts1.length; ++i) pts.push(pts1[i]); for (int i = 0; i &lt; pts2.length; ++i) pts.push(pts2[i]);  pair D = C;  // Select the intersection point that resides inside the triangle for (int i = 0; i &lt; pts.length; ++i) {     if (inTriangle(pts[i], A, B, C)) {         D = pts[i];         break;     } }  // --- Drawing ---  // Draw Triangle and interior lines draw(A--B--C--cycle, linewidth(1)); draw(A--D, linewidth(0.8)); draw(B--D, linewidth(0.8)); draw(C--D, linewidth(0.8));  // Add Points and Labels dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SE, linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, N, linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SW, linewidth(4)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, NE, linewidth(4)); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"258\" />\nWe establish complex coordinates with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e553adc3f3c6ef11722705bda9f18ae8eb7513e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=0, A=1,\\overrightarrow{CB}=b,\\overrightarrow{CD}=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"245\" height=\"24\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6829427883b24f942d2baab56d5ef5d8b5328dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC\\cdot BD=AD\\cdot BC\\iff \\frac{\\lvert\\overrightarrow{DB}\\rvert}{\\lvert\\overrightarrow{DA}\\rvert}=\\frac{\\lvert\\overrightarrow{CB}\\rvert}{\\lvert\\overrightarrow{CA}\\rvert}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"334\" height=\"55\" />, and\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{b-d}{1-d}=\\frac{\\overrightarrow{DB}}{\\overrightarrow{DA}}&amp;=\\frac{\\lvert\\overrightarrow{CB}\\rvert}{\\lvert\\overrightarrow{CA}\\rvert}\\cdot e^{i(\\angle ADB)}\\\\\n&amp;=\\lvert b\\rvert\\cdot e^{i(\\angle ACB)}\\cdot e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\\\\n&amp;=bi\n\\end{align*}\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f033275cdd08fffed439cfd97b940590e33b56e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\frac{b-bi}{1-bi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"85\" height=\"41\" />. We have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be857f766269f17ea0a150340eb0ae6e3601e528.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AB\\cdot CD}{AC\\cdot BD}=\\frac{\\lvert 1-b\\rvert\\lvert d\\rvert}{\\lvert b-d\\rvert}=\\frac{\\lvert 1-b\\rvert\\lvert b-bi\\rvert\\lvert 1-bi\\rvert}{\\lvert 1-bi\\rvert\\lvert bi(1-b)\\rvert}=\\boxed{\\sqrt{2}}\\]\" width=\"417\" height=\"43\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e12f8d4b9001611496ca410ce973317e67716f76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o_1,o_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> be the circumcenters of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f2ecbc73bdcead46cd97ad51a9917b260354ee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD,\\triangle ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />, respectively. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/6/18662820e81aa6b67d528806cb0ff47972f4afc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o_1=\\frac{bd(\\overline{b}-\\overline{d})}{\\overline{b}d-b\\overline{d}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"117\" height=\"46\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28a96c0a8eb9811ea5f7e90c92ca4f5949d633cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1,\\ell_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> be the tangents of the circumcircles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f2ecbc73bdcead46cd97ad51a9917b260354ee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD,\\triangle ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. By the tangency condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/e/c1eace6f7f637a1bd42623fa1ff0029c0bfba3b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o_1\\perp \\ell_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" />, any complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab5f6ab1754aeac40cfac5d4ee795f33dcf9cc89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z\\in\\ell_1 \\setminus \\{0\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f59006b886ba14f5731fdea714d2992e8887fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{z}{o_1}\\in i\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"63\" height=\"37\" />. Hence, the equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff9d2add1273f7f294d4f0318b0ed4340c07768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> can be written as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/f/ecf905629982bf01ab25ba2ad5d2ea2b2ef05f4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{z}{\\overline{z}}=-\\frac{o_1}{\\overline{o_1}}=\\frac{bd(\\overline{b}-\\overline{d})}{\\overline{b}\\overline{d}(b-d)}\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"46\" />\nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/4/c64d20ff7bdc229723d85a38c59062617fbc2dd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1\\| \\,bd(\\overline{b}-\\overline{d})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"23\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e6c135583ab85997b210c2beaaf7a29d6b7d51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_2\\| \\,d(1-\\overline{d})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"23\" />. Thus, it is enough to show that\n\\begin{equation}\n\\frac{b(\\overline{b}-\\overline{d})}{\\overline{b}(b-d)}=-\\frac{1-\\overline{d}}{1-d}\\tag{1}\n\\end{equation}\nSubstituting the expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/3/2c3377cfc915cac715e7e21be34d9b87c0f4343c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{b(\\overline{b}-\\overline{d})}{\\overline{b}(b-d)} = \\frac{b\\cdot\\overline{b}i(\\overline{b}-1)(1-bi)}{(1+\\overline{b}i)\\cdot \\overline{b}\\cdot bi(1-b)} = \\frac{(\\overline{b}-1)(1-bi)}{(1+\\overline{b}i)(1-b)}\\]\" width=\"392\" height=\"46\" />\nEvaluating the RHS yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b853090bd0f3db5c1ad2c3af3267ec5e26a4a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1-\\overline{d}}{1-d}=\\frac{(1-\\overline{b})(1-bi)}{(1+\\overline{b}i)(1-b)}\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"46\" />\nWe see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> holds, as desired.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO\" title=\"1993 IMO\">1993 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017041315\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.149 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 397/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpens